  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation formula\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=0.2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0.2) & ≈\\frac{f(0.2+0.1)-f(0.2)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(0.3)-f(0.2)}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5.8-4.5}{0.1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.3}{0.1} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
